Your apprehension is not without a reason. With the sheer number of
traps in the mines, the probability of a polymorph trap is quite high.
Even if you manage to avoid a polymorph trap, a dwarf or a gnome might
not and could polymorph into, Heavens forbid, a purple lich!

So, I usually do not go past Minetown unless I have intrinsic
telepathy and a towel/blindfold. I put on the towel/blindfold before
proceeding to the next level and check if there are any out-of-depth
monsters. Presence of such a monster, more often than not, means there
is a polymorph trap on that level and I return only after I have magic
resistance.
Of course, this is not a bad strategy to apply to normal dungeon
levels as well but IME, mines are nastier.

This does not protect you from a monster polymorphing when you are
already exploring a level or when you land smack in the middle of
nowhere via a trap door but such things are not completely within your
control.
So take all the precautions you can and hope that worse does not come
to worst.

IMO, lawful characters with Excalibur have a non-trivial advantage in
the Mines, more so past Minetown, with automatic searching and mostly
peaceful monsters. Traps are more easily avoided and only a handful of
hostile monsters need to be focused on. YMMV.

